INSERT INTO public.trustradius_sap_reviews (id, review_url, title, reviewer_name, published_at, rating, pros, cons, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (47, 'https://www.trustradius.com/reviews/sap-analytics-cloud-2026-04-20-06-39-59', 'my honest review about my experience working with SAP Analytics Cloud', 'Verified User', '2026-04-25 15:57:04.244000', 10, e'In my view the best part is self-service functionality for users to create and publish their own dashboard.
With live access from BW4/HANA the authorization from BW is inherited including the analysis authorization.
The unified story is the best thing that was released which provides the option to combine scripting features with graphic design in single version of stories.
The roadmap with SAP Analytics Cloud looks much more exciting with seamless planning with datasphere.
The roadmap of being inclusive in BDC is another best thing looking forward to work with
With the introduction of Joule, the dashboard creation becomes even simpler and this is the best.', e'SAP Analytics Cloud lags in number of chart options provided when we compare with open sources like power BI. I am not saying that it is bad, but most of the end customers make comparison and they always complaint that this was better and easy with power bi
providing more flexibility for merging data from BW systems via live connection and datasphere is something i would like to see.
Though i can combine them at a story level, i would love to see the ability to combine them at single widget level to have data blending/linked analysis.
When new features are released, almost 50% of the time we have defects and we have to raise SAP tickets for resolving them. Testing can be improvised while releasing new features.
The support for analytics query from S4 systems can be accessed directly looks promising. At the same time, i am worried about resilient measures to safeguard the S4 system itself and authorization. The classic world of separate analytical and transactional systems was the best. The more we evolve, the more options, customer wants to have access without understanding the overall strategy and need for different systems', '2026-06-16 14:10:24.531800', '2026-06-16 14:10:24.531800');
